Trim the top-level SUBDIRS to telnet's closure (cosmo only).

inetutils builds all its support libraries and program dirs regardless of
--disable-clients/--disable-servers, which only pick the programs that get
built and installed. libicmp/libls and the ftp/talk/ping/… dirs drag in more
BSD headers cosmo lacks (netinet/in_systm.h, …) for code telnet never links.
Keep exactly gnulib `lib`, libinetutils, libtelnet, the telnet client and
`man` (which installs the prebuilt telnet.1, no help2man run). Dropping `doc`
is also why cosmo.nix collapses the outputs to `out`.

--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -2552,11 +2552,7 @@
 EXTRA_DIST = ChangeLog.0 ChangeLog.1 ChangeLog.2 paths summary.sh.in \
 	CHECKLIST bootstrap bootstrap.conf bootstrap-funclib.sh \
 	$(top_srcdir)/.version
-SUBDIRS = lib \
-	libinetutils libtelnet libicmp libls \
-	src telnet telnetd ftp ftpd talk talkd whois ping ifconfig \
-	doc man \
-	tests
+SUBDIRS = lib libinetutils libtelnet telnet man
 
 DISTCLEANFILES = pathdefs.make paths.defs
 BUILT_SOURCES = $(top_srcdir)/.version
